=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1, dswa1, dswa2
diagnosis_text:
**Affected components:** The Apache2 HTTP daemon on srv1 (10.5.0.4) and the iptables FORWARD policy on dswa1/dswa2.

**Mechanism:** The user's payroll application is a web service that ran on Apache2 on srv1 (10.5.0.4). As of "last night's change," Apache2 is stopped (`inactive dead`); only the BIND DNS daemon (`named`) is still running on that host. Any TCP connection to srv1 on port 80 returns an immediate Connection Refused — the L3 path from pc1 to srv1 is fully intact (4-hop traceroute succeeds, port 53 TCP connects), so the failure is purely at the service layer. This is why ICMP ping to 10.5.0.4 works perfectly while the payroll application is unreachable.

A co-existing fault was also introduced at the same time: both distribution switches for Office A (dswa1 and dswa2) received a pair of iptables FORWARD rules that selectively block **all non-ICMP traffic** from the Office A subnet (10.1.0.0/24) toward the Office B client VLAN (10.3.0.0/24). The first rule explicitly accepts ICMP, causing the ping-based reachability test to show 0% loss to pc3 (10.3.0.100), while TCP/UDP to that subnet times out silently — DROP counters show the rules are actively hitting.

**Localization:** srv1 is the faulty server (Apache2 stopped). dswa1 (br0.10 = 10.1.0.2) and dswa2 (br0.10 = 10.1.0.3) are the faulty distribution switches with the FORWARD drop rules on their br0.10 (VLAN 10) interfaces.

**Root cause:** "Last night's change" stopped the Apache2 web server on srv1 (removing payroll web service from port 80) and simultaneously injected ICMP-bypass drop rules on dswa1/dswa2 blocking TCP/UDP from Office A to Office B's 10.3.0.0/24 VLAN.

**Fix:** Start Apache2 on srv1 (`systemctl start apache2`) to restore the payroll web service. Remove the two injected FORWARD rules from dswa1 and dswa2 (`iptables -D FORWARD -s 10.1.0.0/24 -d 10.3.0.0/24 -i br0.10 -p icmp -j ACCEPT` and `iptables -D FORWARD -s 10.1.0.0/24 -d 10.3.0.0/24 -i br0.10 -j DROP` on each device).
=== END ===